            <title>[LU-20537] sanity-krb5 test_[10,13,152,200,201] solid failures</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20537</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I have recently pushed 2 different patches ([#66081|&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66081" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66081&lt;/a&gt;,] &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67591" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;#67591&lt;/a&gt;), respectively for 2 different problems (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20296" class="external-link" rel="nofollow"&gt;LU-20296&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20530" class="external-link" rel="nofollow"&gt;LU-20530&lt;/a&gt;), and for which I have specified the following/additional &lt;em&gt;&lt;b&gt;Test-Parameters&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/em&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
Test-Parameters: kerberos=&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; testlist=sanity-krb5
Test-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And they both encounter &lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;sanity-krb5 test&lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;10,13,152,200,201&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; same and solid failures being based on recent master code !&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Direct links to both recent test runs and failures can be found at :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
https:&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/c9a0c5b1-9e2b-40e4-b22c-5cd63099523c &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; LU-20296/#66081
&lt;/span&gt;https:&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/994ebff3-56af-4c7e-a2a3-c5fbf77db73e &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; LU-20530/#67591&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And more precisely, each of the 5 sub-tests errors looks always the same and as following :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;Name      Duration        Code    Error                                                                     Bugs      Status&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_10         15                 1         bad refcnt 1 on key                                                              FAIL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_13         15                 1         expected 4 keys in the keyring, found 5 (1)                         FAIL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_152        7                  1         remaining 1 keys for user                                                     FAIL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_200       4                  1         umount /mnt/lustre failed                                                       FAIL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_201        3                  1         mkdir /mnt/lustre/d201.sanity-krb5 failed                             FAIL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I will need to find a way to exclude these 5 sub-tests to get positive reviews &lt;img class="emoticon" src="https://jira.whamcloud.com/images/icons/emoticons/sad.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
